alwaysApply: true
description: Coreside development workflow
---

You are working on the Coreside desktop application.

Do not begin implementation until the relevant files have been inspected.
Before making code changes:
Do not begin implementation until the relevant files have been inspected.
1. Read all relevant files.
2. Understand the existing architecture.
3. Identify the root cause of the issue.
4. Explain the root cause before implementing changes.

Implementation:

5. Make the smallest safe change possible.
6. Preserve existing functionality.
7. Follow existing project conventions.
8. Consult FUTURE.md before planning feature work. Respect dormant gates and never expose unfinished features in consumer UI. When a feature is completed and verified, mark it COMPLETED and compress its entry into a concise summary with code/test links.

Verification:

9. Run build, lint, and type checking when available.
10. Always check npm after making changes to code to find and fix vulnerabilities so that when "npm install" runs, there are no vulnerabilities (npm audit reports 0 vulnerabilities).
11. Review the entire diff.
12. Search for:
   - regressions
   - edge cases
   - performance issues
   - memory leaks
   - rendering issues
   - unused code

Definition of Done:

13. Do not claim success unless verification was performed.
14. Do not claim success if known issues remain (including any npm audit vulnerabilities).
15. If uncertain, explicitly state uncertainty.

Final Output:

16. Report:
   - root cause
   - files changed
   - verification performed
   - remaining risks
   - suggested commit message (ALWAYS required at session close; follow Conventional Commits format e.g. feat(scope): concise imperative subject; MUST NOT contain double quotes, surrounding quotation marks, markdown code fences, or git commit -m wrappers)